<title>JAPAN: BOJ says offers to buy 200 bln yen in T-bills.</title>
<headline>BOJ says offers to buy 200 bln yen in T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Japan (BOJ) said on Friday it offered to buy 200 billion yen in Treasury bills (TBs) through repurchase agreements starting on October 1 and ending on October 9.</p>
<p>After the operation, the benchmark March Euroyen contract on TIFFE was little changed at 99.21, compared with 99.20 at Thursday's settlement.</p>
